## Problem

`inbound_claim` currently only fires for plugin-bound conversations (via `runInboundClaimForPluginOutcome`). Plugins that register global handlers — e.g. listen-only observers, spam filters, rate limiters — are never invoked for unbound inbound events.

Reported in #48434.

## Change

After the `if (pluginOwnedBinding)` block in `dispatch-from-config.ts`, add a single broadcast call to `hookRunner.runInboundClaim()`. This iterates all registered global listeners regardless of conversation binding. If any listener returns `{ handled: true }`, dispatch stops early (same early-return pattern used for plugin-bound handling).

```
+  // Broadcast inbound_claim to global plugin listeners (fixes #48434).
+  if (hookRunner) {
+    const broadcastResult = await hookRunner.runInboundClaim(
+      inboundClaimEvent,
+      inboundClaimContext,
+    );
+    if (broadcastResult?.handled) {
+      markIdle("plugin_broadcast_claim");
+      recordProcessed("completed", { reason: "plugin-broadcast-handled" });
+      return { queuedFinal: false, counts: dispatcher.getQueuedCounts() };
+    }
+  }
```

## Why this is safe

- All supporting infrastructure (`runInboundClaim`, types, runners, event mappers, tests) already exists from PR #45318 — this is purely a missing call-site.
- Backward-compatible: plugins that don't register a global handler are unaffected. The existing plugin-bound flow runs first and is unchanged.
- No new dependencies.

## Testing

Existing tests in `dispatch-from-config.test.ts` and `wired-hooks-inbound-claim.test.ts` cover the runner. I've validated the broadcast path locally against the `openclaw-listen-only` plugin (https://github.com/flowolforg/openclaw-listen-only) on a Telegram group chat.

Closes #48434

Three quick-win fixes following the location icons PR (#127): SVG icons render oversized in flex/grid containers on mobile, student lists sort by insertion order instead of name, and the DataHub classes table lacks color/actions.

## CSS: Location icon sizing (`public/css/styles.css`)
Added explicit size constraints to `.location-icon` to prevent flex/grid stretching:
```css
.location-icon {
    width: 20px; height: 20px;
    max-width: 20px; max-height: 20px;
    overflow: hidden;
}
@media (max-width: 768px) {
    .location-icon { width: 16px; height: 16px; max-width: 16px; max-height: 16px; }
}
```

## Student sorting (`routes/students.js`, `database/repositories/StudentRepository.js`)
- `/students` API now sorts by `name` ASC instead of `student_type`
- `StudentRepository.findAll` always appends `name ASC` as a secondary sort when the primary key isn't `name`, so alphabetical order is preserved within any grouping (e.g., `student_type, name`)
- Attendance matrix already used `ORDER BY student_type, name` — unchanged

## DataHub classes table (`public/js/app.js`)
Enhanced the `classes` column config in `renderCleanTable`:
- Color swatch (10px circle) rendered from the class `color` field (hex-validated before insertion into inline style)
- Rows are now clickable — navigates to the class attendance page
- Added **Actions** column with 📊 View (attendance) and ✏️ Edit buttons
- `viewSearchResult` now handles `type === 'classes'` via `quickAttendanceLink`

